# ─── Rename this file to .env and fill in your values ────────────────────────
# The app works without any keys — it uses mock/demo data by default.

# ─── Clerk Authentication (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# If absent, the app uses localStorage-based mock authentication.
# 1. Create a free account at https://clerk.com
# 2. Create a new application
# 3. Copy your Publishable Key from Clerk Dashboard → API Keys
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ─── Supabase Backend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# If absent, the app uses demo/mock data. No crash, no errors.
# 1. Create a free Supabase project at https://supabase.com
# 2. Go to Project Settings → API
# 3. Copy Project URL and anon/public key below
# 4. Run src/database/schema.sql, then rls-policies.sql, then seed.sql
#
# Phase 4.1 note:
#   Setting these keys enables Supabase connectivity, but project data still
#   uses mock/sessionStorage until Phase 5 wires Clerk JWT into Supabase auth.
#   The "Supabase configured but not connected yet (Phase 5)" banner will show
#   on the Projects page until IS_JWT_READY is set to true in src/lib/supabase.ts.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.xxxxxxxxxxxx

# ─── Supabase Organization ID (optional dev shortcut) ────────────────────────
# Used only for mock data context (role-based project filtering in demo mode).
# NOT used for Supabase authentication — production org resolution requires
# Clerk JWT → Supabase profile mapping (Phase 5).
#
# Find your org UUID after running seed.sql:
#   SELECT id FROM organizations LIMIT 1;
VITE_SUPABASE_ORG_ID=

# ─── ⛔ SERVICE ROLE KEY — NEVER USE IN BROWSER / VITE VARIABLES ─────────────
#
# The Supabase service role key bypasses ALL Row Level Security policies.
# Setting it as a VITE_ variable embeds it in the browser bundle, making it
# visible to anyone who opens DevTools — exposing every row in every table.
#
# ✅ CORRECT usage of the service role key:
#   • In the Supabase SQL Editor (pasting schema.sql, seed.sql, admin queries)
#   • In a secure server-side environment (Node.js backend, Edge Functions)
#   • In local CLI tools: supabase db push, supabase db reset
#
# ❌ NEVER:
#   • Set VITE_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY in .env or any VITE_ variable
#   • Import the service role key in any frontend file
#   • Use the service role key to bypass RLS from the browser
#
# Real database CRUD from the browser requires Phase 5:
#   Clerk JWT → supabase.auth.setSession(clerkToken) → auth.uid() set → RLS works.
